questions.title:
I certify that one or more orientation session(s) was/were conducted by October 31st at which the following information was communicated to all DOE staff, including non-instructional staff: 
 a) The policies and procedures contained in Chancellor's Regulation A-411; 
 b) The contents of the school's Crisis De-escalation Plan; 
 c) The fact that staff must make every effort to de-escalate behavioral crises, where possible, using strategies and interventions for addressing behavioral crises and in-school and community resources identified in the school's Crisis De-Escalation Plan; d) The fact that 911 must be contacted when a student's behavior poses an imminent and substantial risk of injury to himself or others and the situation cannot be safely addressed by school staff or the in-school or community resources identified in the Crisis De-escalation Plan; e) The fact that 911 should not be called in response to a behavioral crisis unless the student's behavior poses an imminent and substantial risk of serious injury to the student and/or others and cannot be safely addressed using deescalation strategies and/or school resources:and f) The fact that opportunities for training on de-escalation may become available throughout the year and staff should contact the principal/designee for further information.
